<title>INDIA: Indian sugar trade remains shut for holiday.</title>
<headline>Indian sugar trade remains shut for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's sugar markets remained closed on Thursday for a local festival and will reopen on Friday, dealers said.</p>
<p>It was closed on Wednesday for a holiday to mark the birth anniversary of a former union leader, they said.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, sugar prices fell by 15/30 rupees per quintal. S-30 ready delivery was quoted at 1,240/1,285 rupees per quintal and M-30 at 1,270/1,320 rupees.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commodities +91-22-265 9000</p>
